 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36023" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5 \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9efb0092-3045-58e2-bed4-ca88fc8fe6c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1074 "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4t \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124951 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124951 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36039" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124951 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124951 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/93/936cea1e20ef7bbc1eb66acf9dd564c61476f5bb68ee05e553b00aaf3f970dc3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible? \n\n- $x\\in [-4,0]$\n- $x\\in (-4,-2]$\n- $x\\in (-3,1)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124951 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8099f21-9137-5121-a075-a61a4c5ae84b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124951 #edb/ref 1074 "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-4,0]$ and $x\\in (-4,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a4/a4499c2d4995c09b9ab6f8852cc2982f415f1650d65429c86df83800344106f4.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1]$  because some lines will intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/cb/cb0a462b3af10d15bb586f127baac45a74eecd5dc19848bda23664e75de968a4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125288 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125288 #edb/ref 1061 11087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125288 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a0c271d5-ca3c-5651-a78d-a2b18242c45c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125288 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125289 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125289 #edb/ref 1061 11090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125289 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9e271cad-793b-51f0-9124-47a943c42f3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125289 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125290 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125290 #edb/ref 1061 11092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125290 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "98229d4f-e216-5858-8b87-e9442dce8ede" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125290 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125291 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125291 #edb/ref 1061 11094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125291 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a9b09430-2391-566d-ac41-6360e135665e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125291 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125297 #edb/ref 1061 11197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125297 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b6bdee